				<title>SCP 5127</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5127</link>
				<description>


&lt;div class=&quot;image-container alignright&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cdn.cheapism.com/images/041918_weird_things_on_amazon_slide_11_fs.max-420x243.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;041918_weird_things_on_amazon_slide_11_fs.max-420x243.jpg&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5127&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5127 is to be contained in a small bag, analyzing the bag has lead to no material that matches. Analyzing SCP-5127 shows the same molecular structure as an normal Banana. SCP-5127 cannot be in distance of any other Bananas, besides the instances it was found with (Aprox. 10 Meters). SCP-5127 is to be binded with its other instances, SCP-5127-A, SCP-5127-B, SCP-5127-C. SCP-5127 must be guarded by Iota-20 (&amp;quot;Mukbang&amp;quot;) at all times, anyone attempting to go near/eat the instances will get shot on sight. SCP-5127 is completely safe, unless not binded with it&#039;s other Bananas, if not bound together, Protocol (&amp;quot;Mukbang&amp;quot;) must be activated. Anyone eating food in the facility is to be stopped on the spot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5127 seems like a normal Banana, not showing signs of nothing different or any mutations, it was found that if you peel SCP-5127-A to C, they will start shaping and mutating, this was just found. SCP-5127 seems to grow some form of fungi on it, and Class-D (&amp;quot;5245&amp;quot;) reported feeling sick after taste testing SCP-5127-B.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5127 also seems to have some form of &amp;quot;Hive&amp;quot; in its middle, as Banana spiders were exiting it. The &amp;quot;Hive&amp;quot; was extracted from SCP-5127-A, and SCP-5127-A was still a normal Banana, but the hive instantly died. This &amp;quot;Hive&amp;quot; seems to duplicate Banana spiders, as there are no way eggs could fit in there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Origin:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5127 was found at a normal walmart in [REDACTED], as employees were reporting seeing large Banana spiders random walk around, this seemed normal at first, but SCP-5127-F (Now gone.) was found and smashed, they saw that spiders were crawling out of its middle. Local County Police gave this over to the SCP Foundation, and gave the SCP Foundation SCP-5127-A to SCP-5127-C, and a sample of SCP-5127-F.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
