					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5655</guid>
				<title>SCP-5655</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5655</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5655&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Containment site lead scientist:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr To██ ███&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special containment procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; scp-5655 is to be kept in its containment cell at all times, any personnel seen trying to move scp-5655 outside of its cell will be terminated immediately. Scp-5655 is to be kept in a glass case which can be easily removed for any tests conducted on scp-5655.&lt;br /&gt;
Scp-5655’s containment cell is to be viewed at all times by the on-site monitoring system, only one armed personnel is required on-site at all times.&lt;br /&gt;
Weekly access to animal remains, D-class personnel remains if necessary, and a wide selection of bones is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; scp-5655 is a sentient human skull made from a substance similar to that of bone. But incredibly more durable than any known earth-based material. Visually scp-5655 is an off creamy colour, with visible cracks, and only 3 teeth missing. Scp-5655 experiences a phenomenon every week on a non-specified day where it completely comes to life and interacts with objects and personnel around it. Scp-5655 claims to be able to see, hear, smell and taste, many tests have taken place to prove this, and all have been proven true.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the phenomenon scp-5655 asks for nothing but bones and refuses to answer any questions before being provided with bones, Dr H█████ Atlis has decided bones are to be given to scp-5655 when asked, but to dispose of all bones before scp-5655&#039;s phenomenon is over. Scp-5655 is able to make any personnel bring him what he wants, it is believed scp-5655 excretes a form of hypnosis over affected personnel, it also attempts to persuade individuals itself with very unconvincing arguments, but with the hypnosis in effect scp-5655 exclusively thinks its simply very convincing. Scp-5655 speaks in a very polite tone, similar to that of a father speaking to his son. It is unknown whether this is an act or not. Personnel affected by this form of hypnosis describes scp-5655 as bright white in colour, no missing teeth, no cracks or dents, and a faint smell of lavender emanating from it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When bones are given to scp-5655 it is able to hold and connect them together with small fleshy tendrils that extrude from the foramen magnum at the bottom of the skull. Scp-5655 is able to connect these bone pieces together and form a rudimentary skeleton, it is important to note that the origin of each bone will not affect scp-5655’s construction ability, it is able to use this skeleton to become mobile, but Dr H█████ Atlis has limited the amount of time scp-5655 is able to use the bones to five minutes, as not to give a feeling of freedom, one the bones are removed from scp-5655’s cell it begins to shout profanities at personnel until the phenomenon is over.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When scp-5655 is dormant, personnel continuously report that scp-5655 is watching them, or that they see it blink, when in a dormant state scp-5655 is to be considered hostile, as scp-5655 is only harmless during its once a week phenomenon. Many personnel are effected by scp-5655’s hypnosis in its supposed dormant state, but only a few are spoken to by it, when being spoken to by scp-5655 personnel report being asked about themselves, and eventually being asked to give their skin and flesh to scp-5655, personnel affected by this begin ripping off their own skin and flesh and will only be stopped by being completely restrained, while being questioned about this, affected personnel describes scp-5655 being in disarray, with teeth missing, holes and cracks everywhere, with the skull almost being completely black in colouring, the bone-like texture now being similar to that of rusted metal, rotting flesh is also smelled by the affected personnel, and doesn&#039;t become weaker or stronger if moving. The voice being heard is described as if it came from a faraway siren, and not directly from scp-5655 itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional notes:&lt;/strong&gt; Scp-5655 was put into foundation containment on 17/6/20██ it was found in the small town of ██████, Alaska, local police reports tell of disturbing sights In an abandoned construction site on the south side of town, with residents finding large mounds of flesh and bone all surrounding a single skull in the center of the mass.&lt;br /&gt;
Agents arrived and retrieved scp-5655 from the construction site with no resistance&lt;br /&gt;
Scp-5655 has been moved to a US site in Dallas Texas, site-██ as a part of a new facility centered around scp-xxxx(my first scp).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following interviews and report logs were conducted by Dr H█████ Atlis/ Dr B████:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-1&quot;&gt;interview/report log 1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-2&quot;&gt;interview/report log 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-3&quot;&gt;interview/report log 3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-4&quot;&gt;interview/report log 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-5&quot;&gt;interview/report log 5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-final-log&quot;&gt;interview/report final log&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607351682&quot; alt=&quot;Sami Gibbons&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;Sami Gibbons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
