						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5441</p> <p><strong>Object class:</strong> Keter</p> <p><strong>Containment site lead scientist:</strong> Dr To██ ███</p> <p><strong>Special containment procedures:</strong> scp-5441 cannot be contained, only monitored, personnel who are apart of scp-5441’s research team are to monitor all activity on scp-5441-1, and to report if any instances of scp-5441-3 are seen on scp-5441-1 or on research stations.<br /> Scp-5441-1 is to only be boarded when approved by higher ups in the foundation, with a fully armed response team on standby in any case.<br /> Scp-5441-2 is to be kept in a locked safe behind the code ██████ in Dr Oman's personal research wing.<br /> Scp-5441-3 is to only be viewed, but not engaged, it is still believed to be safe, but more information is required to properly judge its threat class</p> <p>All personnel working on scp-5441 are to be mentally assessed weekly and research findings checked daily</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> scp-5441 is a body of water like substance of an undetermined size, and an immeasurable depth, many samples of scp-5441 have been collected from inside the containment zone, all results so far have come back as negative to any foreign bodies present in the water, further research is required.<br /> Scp-5441 is believed to be sentient, or at least appears to be sentient, and has the ability to influence the mind of individuals with prolonged exposure to it.</p> <p>Scp-5441-1 is an oil rig at the center of the containment zone, the platform is unregistered to any existing company, and no such building plans, or permits are in existence, it is unknown where, or how this oil platform came to be.<br /> Expeditions onto scp-5441-1 have determined the platform is long abandoned, with all sources of rations depleted, and the entire lower deck gone, presumably ripped off by natural causes.</p> <p>Scp-5441-2 is an incomplete collection of log entries found onboard scp-5441-1 in what once was the crew's sleeping quarters. The notes make mention of there being at least 28 logs, over the course of 30 days, but only 10 have been successfully discovered and retrieved.<br /> scp-5441-2 seems to have been hand written by an unknown individual, but it is presumed they were terminated, most likely drowned.<br /> It is unknown whether scp-5441-3 had anything to do with the termination of the author, yet there is no signs that scp-5441-3 is even able to hold physical objects, further tests required.</p> <p>Scp-5441-3 are a humanoid being made of the same substance as scp-5441, further research is required to determine whether scp-5441-3 is just a humanoid form of scp-5441, or if they're their own entity entirely.<br /> They have been seen with the ability to navigate scp-5441-1 without any difficulty, personnel have also reported seeing them on the research platform surrounding the containment site, the containment of instances of scp-5441-3 is near impossible, as when all leading paths are blocked off for scp-5441-3, it just dissolves and finds its way back to scp-5441.<br /> Attempts to communicate with scp-5441-3 have all failed, but personnel report feeling safe when around them, and not wanting to leave it. Scp-5441-3 also seems to be safe for the most part, but unknown if they can be provoked or not.</p> <p><strong>Additional notes:</strong> scp-5441 was first discovered by the foundation on the 15/11/20██ when a category five storm subsided in the northern pacific ocean, where an unregistered abandoned oil rig was detected by the foundation, with a small recovery team sent in to investigate only a day later, the mission was successful in the recovery of scp-5441-2, and the discovery of over 10 instances of scp-5441-3. Dr To██ ███, the head of site-██ requested a detachment of his Dallas Texas site be used to contain the anomaly, with his request being granted by higher ups in the foundation.</p> <hr /> <h1><span>SCP-5441-2 Archived Journal Entries:</span></h1> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 1:</strong> I don't know what happened, or where I am, for god sake, I don't even know my own name, but I thought writing a daily journal may keep me sane, for the time being at least. I've only been here for.. Well what I hope is two days, that's when I woke up at least. I'm on some sort of oil rig, or something like it, it looks old, and long abandoned, but I never feel alone, it's like…. It's like the water is watching me.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 2:</strong> the platform seems to have been abandoned for months, or even years. There isn't much food left, maybe only enough for a month maybe? I don't know, I decided to set up camp in there, probably my best chance of survival. Another thing, I haven't seen any fish, or well, anything in the water the entire time, there's no waves, no water current or anything, it's just… still. I'm sure that I'm not alone out here.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 4:</strong> thought I was done for when that wave came, after basically five days of nothing a wave almost the size of this oil rig completely ripped off the bottom deck, I don't know what happened or what it was, but I was warned, the water, it spoke to me, no.. no it can't be, what am I even saying.. It's just my common sense of course. I may just need some sleep after that.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 5:</strong> I finally saw something today, a man or well a clear, water looking thing in the shape of a man, he was sitting on a piece of driftwood but too far out to see properly. I wasn't frightened though or even on edge, he waved at me, and I waved back, I almost felt.. Safe. nothing else really happened, foods running low, I'm not sure how long it'll last. But these daily logs are the only thing keeping me sane.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 8:</strong> the water men come aboard sometimes, I see them walking around, they don't bother me though, and they feel like.. my friends. The last of the rations will only last another day, but the water tells me it will help.. I still don't know what to think, but I feel like I can trust them, I feel like I can join them.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 12:</strong> the sea water wasn't as bad as I feared, it worked, it even tasted.. good in a way, it quenched my thirst, and even my hunger, I don't know how that works, but it did. One of the water men came to me and walked with me throughout the day, he seemed.. friendly, and I felt I could trust him, and the water even more, the voices of the sea don't scare me anymore.. but they only want one thing from me, they want me to swim with them, to find the ocean surface, but that's too much for me right now.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 17:</strong> I find myself swimming just off of the platform more of the time than before, the pull from the water is growing, and I sometimes think that it might be safer down there, safer with them. The water men go back to the ocean when it's night, sometimes it feels like they ask me to follow, but I can't… just not yet.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 18:</strong> more water men came today, almost twice as many I think, they seem.. more human, and I can sometimes even see them smile when they see me. The water has begun to move, waves forming, and I sometimes see what I can only assume is an entrance, an entrance to peace, where the water men come from.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 22:</strong> I'm swimming deeper, deeper into peace, but I always float back to the surface, I'm not ready. the water men speak to me sometimes, almost trying to convince me to join them, and follow them after dark, they tell me only to follow when I'm ready, when I can experience peace.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Daily journal entry 28:</strong> I have seen it, I have found my peace, the water, it embraces me, the water men, my friends. I finally followed the water men, and they were my guide in peace and they helped me. They pulled me deeper, deeper into the water, and when I woke up.. I saw it, they showed me. if my messages find anyone, please, please join us, join within the water. It will save you, and bring you peace.</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <p><strong>missing journal entries listed below:</strong><br /> entry 3-6-7-9-10-11-13-14-15-16-19-20-21-23-24-25-26-27</p> <h4><span><strong>Further research and possible expeditions required to make appropriate judgment on specified SCP</strong></span></h4> <hr /> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607351682" alt="Sami Gibbons" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" >Sami Gibbons</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
