				<title>SCP-5295</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5295</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5295&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5295 is to be kept in a locked box to prevent unauthorised reading unless being used for testing. During testing, SCP-5295 and at least 5 D-Class personnel must be locked in a standard humanoid containment cell to prevent SCP-5295-1 from breaching containment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5295 is an anomalous fiction storybook that changes it&#039;s content every 5-7 days. When SCP-5295 is read by a human the first 3-5 chapters will seem normal compared to an average storybook but all chapters after chapter 5 have been recorded to become darker and more of a horror story. These chapters have been named the &amp;quot;Devil&#039;s chapters&amp;quot;. When a human begins to read the Devil&#039;s chapters their mental state instantly starts to deteriorate. The more that is read, the quicker the deterioration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5295 will start to mention SCP-5295-1 in chapter 10 and more frequently in chapters following chapter 10. SCP-5295-1 is a humanoid entity created by SCP-5295 that appears in the book and is described in SCP-5295&#039;s pages to kill at least 3 humans in gruesome detail. Its appearance can be widely varied but all previous testing has shown it to take a humanoid form. SCP-5295-1 will appear in the reader&#039;s dreams, the frequency of it appearing depends on how much of SCP-5295 was read.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As soon as the last chapter has been read (assuming all other chapters have also been read) the reader will instantly have a severe stroke and die. Within 2 minutes of the reader&#039;s death, SCP-5295-1 will begin to emerge from the readers head and proceed to kill the same number of humans as SCP-5295 described it to in the chapters proceeding chapter 10. After all the required humans have been killed the entity will return to SCP-5295 and seemingly merge with the book. All attempts to prevent SCP-5295-1 from killing humans have been unsuccessful. All attempts to prevent SCP-5295-1 from returning to SCP-5295 have been unsuccessful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery Log&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5295 was recovered in Utah where multiple people were being found massacred with a storybook found close to them. A recovery team retrieved SCP-5295 and brought it back to the facility for testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breach log&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5295-1 breached containment when it was required to kill 10 humans. The entity was able to kill all 10 humans in 6 minutes and 32 seconds. It then returned to SCP-5295 and merged with it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5294&quot;&gt;SCP-5294&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-5295 | &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5296&quot;&gt;SCP-5296&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-j-mckeown&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7065144&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607351682&quot; alt=&quot;Dr J McKeown&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7065144)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-j-mckeown&quot;  &gt;Dr J McKeown&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
