												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Final Documented Instance Of SCP-5655’s Weekly Phenomenon:</strong></p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr B████</p> <p><strong>Interviewee:</strong> scp-5655</p> <p><strong>Date/s:</strong> 29/8/20██</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>[BEGIN LOG]</strong></p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong>… I see, all of you…. Dr B, you will always disappoint me</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> hello scp-5655, my goal isn't to impress you, so your disappointment is only noted.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> you should never disappoint your guest…</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> noted, on more pressing matters, why have you been dormant for more than a month, and where, if anywhere, have you been.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong>…. I watched all of you, especially you Dr B&#8230;. and I waited.</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> I thought your sentience was only during your phenomenon?</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong>… Aha it is</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> then how could you-</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> NO MATTER, enough of that foolery, I think you have an idea of what I'm pondering on now</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> uh, yes, we know what you want (away from mic) send in D-95714, and give him the remains of Dr Atlis.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> uh, no wait, what did you just say champ?</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> the bones are being sent in momentarily, have some patience.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> oh. Well alright!</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> hel… Hello scp-5655, I have uh, I have your bones.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> aha you D class personnel are always good lads I-</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong>…. These bones, they're…. ahem, Mr D-95 whatever, I have another request for you</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> I… I don't think I'm allowed to do anything else…. I.. I'm sorry</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> c'mon lad, I'm sure you don't want to disappoint your guest would ya?</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> I'm just not….. No, no you make some good points, I… I think I'm allowed to make one more request, surely</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> good… aha, now, I want you to take me out of this cell….. Bring me to Dr B, and give me his flesh, and bone…. ahem, did you get that champ?</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> yes…. yes I did…. And It would be my honour to bring you what you need</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> Subject D-95714 any action you take that is not a part of procedure will be considered hostile, and you will be promptly terminated, do you understand?</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> NO!&#8230;. I can't disappoint him, he… he knows what's best, and you're nothing but… but flesh and bone for him</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong> I repeat, Subject D-95714 any action you take that is not a part of procedure will be considered hostile, and you will be promptly terminated, do you understand?</p> <p><strong>D-95714:</strong> No oh god no please don't do this, I can't disobey him…. He'll be disappointed in me! Please, please give him your flesh, he deserves it, he needs it!</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong>…. Bring me to the cell door, now</p> <p><strong>Description of current events:</strong><br /> Subject D-95714 proceeds to remove scp-5655's glass casing and then lifts it up and cradles it in his arms, he keeps repeating the phrase &quot;he deserves it, he deserves it&quot; subject D-95714 then runs to the cell door and starts violently slamming his left arm on the door, so hard his arm begins breaking.</p> <p><strong>Subject D-95714:</strong> please let me out! Oh god please, I can't handle this…… he.. He needs your flesh doctor! Please, your bones too!</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> use door code ████</p> <p><strong>Subject D-95714:</strong> okay. okay I will..</p> <p><strong>Description of current events:</strong><br /> The containment cell door slides open with Subject D-95714 quickly sprinting out of the cell door, heading straight for Dr B, armed personnel are quick to respond, instantly shooting D-95714 in the cranium, with him dropping to the floor, and scp-5655 dropping with him. but with it falling directing facing Dr B.</p> <p><strong>Dr B:</strong>&#8230;.. You over there, pick it up, pick it up now. And put it back in that fucking containment cell now!</p> <p><strong>scp-5655:</strong>…. You will never contain me Dr B…. never destroy me….. your research, never finished&#8230;… and you all will never know why I was here…. Goodbye B████, I trust my time here was…….. entertaining.</p> <p><strong>[END LOG]</strong></p> </blockquote> <hr /> <h2><span><strong>IMPORTANT ANY FURTHER COMMUNICATION WITH SCP-5655 IS TO BE REPORTED TO DR B████ EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY</strong></span></h2> <p><strong>Post interview report</strong><br /> This is will likely be the final report on scp-5655, for while at least. the thing has stopped talking to us, and we believe it's attempt to escape was more a warning rather than an actual escape plan, but we may never know, research on scp-5655 will continue, but with no knew information many of our personnel may be reassigned to other anomalies, as scp-5655 may stay in its dormant state forever.</p> <p><strong>Signing off:</strong> Dr B████</p> <hr /> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607351684" alt="Sami Gibbons" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" >Sami Gibbons</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
