				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-4</guid>
				<title>Interview Report Log 4</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/interview-report-log-4</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fourth documented instance of scp-5655’s weekly phenomenon:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr H█████ Atlis&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewee:&lt;/strong&gt; scp-5655&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Date/s:&lt;/strong&gt; 16/7/20██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[BEGIN LOG]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; Mr Doctor, can you hear me?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes scp-5655 we can hear you, welcome back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; Ah splendid! Now, how has the foundation been?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; Sorry, the foundation?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; Ahah, you always make me laugh lad! But I&#039;ve done a bit of nosing around a bit myself, and i&#039;m far more well acquainted with the overall establishment I&#039;ve found myself in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; if you wouldn&#039;t mind me asking, but how in hell did you get access to the foundations database? Your containment cell doesn&#039;t even receive cell phone reception.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; Oh keep up Dr Atlis, I&#039;ve told you I&#039;m only here one day a week, you expected me not to find out what my new home is ahah. Now now, I&#039;m curious about some of the other guests of this place, you hear me champ? Of course only the ones with a reputation Ahaha&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; okay, I&#039;ll make you a deal scp-5655, I will tell you information that security level 1 personnel are given access too&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; that&#039;ll do for me, now I won&#039;t waste your time, I&#039;ll settle for information on one, scp-049&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; oh uh, scp-049, at least we know you didn’t dig too far in our files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; Ahah yeahh, now now, I&#039;m mainly interested in the thing he refers to as “the pestilence”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; oh, the pestilence, we don&#039;t know much about it, but we believe he&#039;s referring to the black plague, but he-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; The black plague you say! I remember that almost as it was yesterday!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; …. You were around in the 13 hundreds?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; well yes of course! Quite an enjoyable time to finally visit this reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; reality?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; aha yeah! Anywho, I was hoping to arrange a meeting with ol 049, would you kindly grant my request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; sorry scp-5655, meetings with 049 are strictly prohibited, and I&#039;m sure 049 wouldn&#039;t take kindly to any new residents of the foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; we would be happy to grant any other request, within reason of course.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; you&#039;re a good man Mr doctor, but as always, I would kindly request some bones!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; we can gladly accept that (backs away from mic) send in the cow remains&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; ahah I know what ya doing, testing my abilities right?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; we need to conduct research somehow, I&#039;m sure you understand scp-5655?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; of course of course (focus on entrance) Ah! Here&#039;s my bones, now let me get to work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;description of current events&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Scp-5655 then proceeds to once again grow its fleshy tendrils, but thicker and longer, perhaps in an attempt to compensate for the larger profile of the prescribed bones. It attaches the bones in a vaguely humanoid shape, far from the actual stature of a cow, scp-5655 then stands up with the newly constructed skeleton and looks directly at Dr Atlis, with far more precision than previous, almost like there are eyes in the skulls sockets that are unseen by personnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; actually, i do have a question, how are you able to keep the bones connected? You don&#039;t seem to wrap them in those fleshy cords you have, they&#039;re just….. floating&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; sorry, but I&#039;m having a hard time understanding you, i simply connected them to each other aha&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; but they&#039;re flo……… you know what, it doesn&#039;t matter, I&#039;ve been informed to tell you to stay out of classified foundation files, failure to comply with this order will result in loss of current privileges, for example, ill have to stop granting your request for bones, do you understand?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scp-5655:&lt;/strong&gt; oh boo, I&#039;m simply trying to make my stay enjoyable, The 05 council apparently never lets anyone have any fun around here I-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Atlis:&lt;/strong&gt; knowledge of the 05 council is strictly prohibited! This interview is over (away from mic) shut off all vocal feeds now, and I want the incinerator turned on immediately!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;description of current events&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The incinerator is turned on at a higher temperature than recommended, the reinforced glass window of scp-5655’s containment cell begins showing signs of damage before being turned off, scp-5655 is once again viewed undamaged, and back in its glass case.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[END LOG]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post interview report&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Scp-5655 is now to be considered a massive security breach risk to the foundation, the 05 council have been directly informed about the classified information known by scp-5655. I just, I&#039;m not sure what they&#039;ll do, i don&#039;t know if I&#039;m gonna be fired, or well, worse. This scp was under my control and I basically let it breach containment and find out so much about the foundation, and even my own name. Anyway, further testing will take place, and everything scp-5655 is and isn&#039;t capable of will be found, and used against it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Signed:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr H█████ Atlis&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607351684&quot; alt=&quot;Sami Gibbons&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;Sami Gibbons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 07 Dec 2020 10:28:07 +0000</pubDate>
