						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Fourth documented instance of scp-5655’s weekly phenomenon:</strong></p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr H█████ Atlis</p> <p><strong>Interviewee:</strong> scp-5655</p> <p><strong>Date/s:</strong> 16/7/20██</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>[BEGIN LOG]</strong></p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> Mr Doctor, can you hear me?</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> Yes scp-5655 we can hear you, welcome back.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> Ah splendid! Now, how has the foundation been?</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> Sorry, the foundation?</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> Ahah, you always make me laugh lad! But I've done a bit of nosing around a bit myself, and i'm far more well acquainted with the overall establishment I've found myself in.</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> if you wouldn't mind me asking, but how in hell did you get access to the foundations database? Your containment cell doesn't even receive cell phone reception.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> Oh keep up Dr Atlis, I've told you I'm only here one day a week, you expected me not to find out what my new home is ahah. Now now, I'm curious about some of the other guests of this place, you hear me champ? Of course only the ones with a reputation Ahaha</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> okay, I'll make you a deal scp-5655, I will tell you information that security level 1 personnel are given access too</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> that'll do for me, now I won't waste your time, I'll settle for information on one, scp-049</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> oh uh, scp-049, at least we know you didn’t dig too far in our files.</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> Ahah yeahh, now now, I'm mainly interested in the thing he refers to as “the pestilence”</p> <p><strong>Dr Atlis:</strong> oh, the pestilence, we don't know much about it, but we believe he's referring to the black plague, but he-</p> <p><strong>Scp-5655:</strong> The black plague you say!