				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5212-expedition-2</guid>
				<title>SCP-5212 Expedition 2</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5212-expedition-2</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Date:&lt;/strong&gt; 15-7-20██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approved by:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. To██ ███.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subject/s:&lt;/strong&gt; two subjects have been selected to enter scp-5212, D-24576-A male, 36yrs and D-8697-B male, 24yrs. Both have been equipped with a headset with a built in camera, a satchel bag, a hand held torch, and a small bottle of water.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Both subjects are instructed to enter scp-5212, with the front door being left open, the two are then instructed to take the same course as the previous expedition but to make a slight deviation into one of the rooms. The two then enter one of the rooms in the longer hallway, with the camera picking up another hallway inside of the room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Both subjects are to make an effort in finding more textbooks amongst the clutter. Subject A then finds one, with subject A being ordered to return to control with his find. Subject B is to continue deeper into scp-5212-1. Subject 2 protests at first, but control convinces him to proceed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject B carries on through the hallway, control then orders them to take a sample of the wall material. Subject B comments on the density of the wall, and that a piece cannot be removed. Control then instructs them to find a piece that&#039;s already broken off, but this request is not carried through as there is no indication of damage to any of the walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject B is then ordered to proceed to the end of the hallway, with the camera looking out for any indication of hand written notes. Once subject B gets to the end, he finds a T junction. The right hallway is viewed to have another T junction at its end, while the left has a closed door. Control then orders them to proceed to the closed door.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject B is then instructed to open the door, they comply and open it, but are stopped when the door doesn&#039;t open out fully. They try to open it with more force, but it still doesn&#039;t open. Control instructs him to see what is keeping it closed, Subject B begins to panic, with the camera showing an unidentifiable hand holding the other doorknob. The door slams shut, control orders them to try and open it again, Subject B is still panicking, and asks to leave, control accepts his request but instructs him to search for more writing of any sort.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject B is not successful in acquiring anything. Control then instructs them to return to the start of the T junction, they then reach the junction, but the hallway now leads to the entrance, where control orders him to exit scp-5212. The front door is shut behind him.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post expedition report:&lt;/strong&gt; Subject D-24576-A retrieved another textbook, illustrations now included, showing a ball, a shoe, and coin. Subject D-8697-B did not retrieve anything, however the discovery of scp-5212-2 has now completely changed our approach towards scp-5212. We now also believe these notes we have picked up have been written by scp-5212-2 More evidence now suggests that scp-5212-1 is intentionally leading subjects out of the house, motive still unknown.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Signed:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. To██ ███.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607351684&quot; alt=&quot;Sami Gibbons&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons&quot;  &gt;Sami Gibbons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 07 Dec 2020 10:45:32 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
